  "chapter": {
    "number": 16,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          { "text": "Send rams to the ruler of the land", "poem": 1 },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "from Selah in the wilderness, to the mount of the daughter of Zion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          { "text": "As wandering birds, as a scattered nest,", "poem": 1 },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "so the women of Moab are at the fords of the Arnon River.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "“Give instruction, execute justice; provide some shade like night in the middle of the day;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "hide the fugitives; do not betray the fugitives.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them live among you, the refugees from Moab;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "be a hiding place for them from the destroyer.”",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "For the oppression will stop, and destruction will cease,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "those who trample will disappear from the land.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A throne will be established in covenant faithfulness; and one from David's tent will faithfully sit there.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "He will judge as he seeks justice and does righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We have heard of Moab's pride, his arrogance,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "his boasting, and his anger. But his boastings are empty words.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So Moab wails for Moab—they all wail! Mourn, you who are utterly destroyed, for the raisin cakes of Kir Hareseth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The fields of Heshbon have dried up as well as the vines of Sibmah.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "The rulers of the nations have trampled the choice vines",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "that reached to Jazer and spread into the desert.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "Its shoots spread abroad; they went over to the sea.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Indeed I will weep along with Jazer for the vineyard of Sibmah.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "I will water you with my tears, Heshbon, and Elealeh.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "For on your fields of summer fruits and harvest I have ended the shouts of joy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Gladness and joy are taken away from the fruit tree groves; and there is no singing, or shouts in the vineyards.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "No one treads out wine in the presses, for I have put an end to the shouts of the one who treads.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So my heart sighs like a harp for Moab, and my inward being for Kir Hareseth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When Moab wears himself out on the high place",
            "poem": 1
          },
          { "lineBreak": true },
          {
            "text": "and enters his temple to pray, his prayers will accomplish nothing.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "This is the word that Yahweh spoke concerning Moab previously."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "Again Yahweh speaks, “Within three years, the glory of Moab will disappear; in spite of his many people, the remnant will be very few and insignificant.”"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
